WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.437
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:05.124
An instance brought to the
Entra-exclusive posture can slide back.

3
00:00:05.124 --> 00:00:07.881
An administrator can
switch it to mixed mode,

4
00:00:07.881 --> 00:00:10.563
create a SQL login, or
add a Windows login.

5
00:00:10.563 --> 00:00:12.862
So closure isn't a one-time action.

6
00:00:12.862 --> 00:00:15.826
It's a record that keeps coming
back clean on a schedule,

7
00:00:15.826 --> 00:00:17.538
and drift is the run that doesn't.

8
00:00:17.538 --> 00:00:21.748
In this module you project an audit
run onto the five closure conditions,

9
00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:24.554
see which fields the audit
can't settle by itself,

10
00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:27.501
and compare two runs so a
regression becomes a task.
